# Figure Specification: Dual Regime Mapping

Title: Dual-Regime Mapping of Dimensional Cores

Layout:
- Two side-by-side vertical panels, left = RTT, right = vST.
- A shared central band showing the dimensional primitive set P.
- Arrows from both regime anchors into the shared primitive set.

Left Panel (RTT):
- Header: "Resonance-Time (RTT)"
- Anchor box labeled "T_r"
- Under the anchor, a small note: "resonance-time anchor"
- Arrow from T_r into the central primitive band.

Right Panel (vST):
- Header: "Validated Spacetime (vST)"
- Anchor box labeled "S_r"
- Under the anchor, a small note: "validated spacetime anchor"
- Arrow from S_r into the central primitive band.

Center Band:
- Large box labeled "Shared Dimensional Primitive Set P"
- Inside the box: "D3  D4  D5  D6  D7  D8  D9"
- Beneath the primitives: "Triadic Operators: merge, split, corridor, loop, anchor"
- Beneath that: "Validation Layer: corridors + loops"

Bottom Caption:
"Dimensional cores, operators, and validation structures remain invariant under
regime substitution. Only the declared anchor differs."
